20:14.040 --> 20:24.040
The role of the adversary changes in the sense that the adversary is still there because, and it can see some things, but not everything.

20:24.040 --> 20:29.040
So what a randomized algorithm processes is that you write down your algorithm description.

20:29.040 --> 20:37.040
The adversary gets to see that description and choose potentially a really bad instance given that description.

20:37.040 --> 20:47.040
But what the adversary does not see is that it doesn't see what are those random points that you're throwing as you go along.

20:47.040 --> 20:51.040
So the random bits, those are not visible to the adversary.

20:51.040 --> 21:03.040
